From efd6f6a9b71d4289e7426a470dd815749136d10a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:49:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Dynamics: each animation slot's chain-joint counts
 translated as the file's words, not as null pointers

ftDynamics.x10 is declared FigaTree***, but each relocated slot of its
table points at plain 32-bit counts: how many leading chain joints the
animation drives. ftCo_8009E4A8 and ftCo_8009E7B4 hand tree[i] to
ftCo_8009CB40, which compares it as (s32) arg3 against the chain index.
The counts are not relocated, so the hosted native-DAT translation, which
follows the declared pointer type, made every one NULL (0) and every chain
joint was solved by physics (Peach, Zelda, Donkey Kong, Marth, Roy).

The translation now keeps the declared host shape (pointer-sized slots)
and carries each count in its slot as the PPC word; a slot without a
relocation stays NULL. Kirby's hats keep x10 raw (MslDatKirbyHatDynamics).
PPC builds are unchanged. This changes hosted gameplay wherever an
animation drives part of a chain, so the replay gate and output locks need
a run with game data.

dynamics-counts-smoke translates a synthetic ftDataCaptain (no game data)
and checks the counts; it fails without the change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
